- layouts/sumi.json: a clone of the shipped main layout. Modified: it adds the
  ink block beside the terminals, points the sidebar's spaces and agents blocks
  at sumi-spaces and sumi-agents, sets the theme, the UI font and a settings
  picture, drops the root divider, and changes the work area's padding and gap
  and the pane frames' radius, focus color and lone setting.
- mods/sumi-spaces: a clone of the shipped spaces mod. Modified, in its drawing
  only: ink letter stamps (outlined, filled for the active space) instead of
  colored chips; the ahead/behind counts, the connection badge, the login and
  reconnect warnings, the rail's status glyph and the drag line in ink tones
  instead of status colors; 2 px corners.
- mods/sumi-agents: a clone of the shipped agents mod. Modified, in its drawing
  only: ink status marks (a breathing dot for working, an empty red square and
  "needs you" for blocked, a filled red square for done, a pale ring for idle)
  instead of the spinner, the tinted badges and the status-colored dot; group
  headings and the folded sub-agent count in ink; 2 px corners; its sort menu
  opens this mod (the overlay name mod.clone rewrites).

The layout-node lookup in mods/ink-painting/main.js (find, in fold) is
adapted from the one in the workspace-chrome and tabs mods shipped with the
Herdr app; modified.

The layout's other mods (workspace-chrome, tabs, pane, files, changes and
workspace-status), the menu the spaces list opens, and the icons the lists draw
from mods/workspace-chrome/ are the Herdr app's own, used from the person's
install; they are not copied here.

The ink painting's drawing code is original. Sumi bundles no fonts and no
images from elsewhere: every stroke, seal, square and paper texture is an SVG
the mod writes at run time, layouts/sumi.svg is the layout's own settings
picture, and the UI font, Hiragino Mincho ProN, is the one macOS provides.
